.el .ds Aq '
.TH hopback 1  "hopback 0.2.0" 
.SH NAME
hopback \- Find, resume and fork coding\-agent sessions across Claude Code, Codex and more
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBhopback\fR [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-agent\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-directory\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR] [\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-offset\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-refresh\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-hidden\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-messages\fR] [\fB\-\-rebuild\fR] [\fB\-\-stats\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\-context\fR] [\fB\-\-print\fR] [\fB\-\-yolo\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIQUERY\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find, resume and fork coding\-agent sessions across Claude Code, Codex and more
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-agent\fR \fI<AGENT>\fR
Filter by agent id
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-directory\fR \fI<DIRECTORY>\fR
Filter by working directory substring
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
List matching sessions instead of opening the TUI
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
List sessions and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print matching sessions as one JSON object and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<N>\fR
Maximum sessions to return (default: 50 for \-\-json, 200 for \-\-list)
.TP
\fB\-\-offset\fR \fI<N>\fR
Skip this many matches
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Return every match from the requested offset
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-refresh\fR
Serve the existing index without scanning agent files
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-hidden\fR
Include sessions hidden in hopback in \-\-json and \-\-list output
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-messages\fR
Include the conversation text of each session in \-\-json output
.TP
\fB\-\-rebuild\fR
Drop and reconstruct the index from agent files
.TP
\fB\-\-stats\fR
Show the statistics dashboard and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\-context\fR
Print instructions for coding agents that want to use hopback, and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-print\fR
Print the folder and the resume command instead of running it
.TP
\fB\-\-yolo\fR
Launch with the agent\*(Aqs skip\-permission flags where supported
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIQUERY\fR] [default: ]
Search text plus keyword filters, or `.` to resume the newest session of the current folder
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
hopback\-fork(1)
Fork an existing session into a fresh one
.TP
hopback\-pin(1)
Pin a session to the top of the list
.TP
hopback\-unpin(1)
Remove a session\*(Aqs pin
.TP
hopback\-rename(1)
Give a session a title inside hopback
.TP
hopback\-hide(1)
Hide a session from hopback
.TP
hopback\-unhide(1)
Show a hidden session again
.TP
hopback\-completions(1)
Print a shell completion script
.TP
hopback\-man(1)
Print the man page in roff format
.TP
hopback\-config(1)
Manage hopback configuration
.TP
hopback\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.0
